          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 3-year-old child with moderate persistent asthma needs daily inhaled corticost</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 3-year-old child with moderate persistent asthma needs daily inhaled corticosteroid therapy. Which device and technique is most appropriate?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Dry powder inhaler with coaching on forceful inhalation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Dry powder inhalers require a strong, rapid inspiratory effort to aerosolise the medication — a skill beyond children under 6–8 years of age.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Jet nebuliser for every scheduled dose</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Nebulisers are reserved for acute severe episodes or when spacer use is impractical. For daily maintenance, they are less portable and no more effective than the correct alternative.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pressurised metered-dose inhaler actuated directly into the mouth</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Without a spacer, most of the aerosol impacts the oropharynx rather than reaching the lower airways, and coordinating actuation with inhalation is impossible at this age.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pressurised metered-dose inhaler with a spacer and face mask</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>For children below 5–6 years, a pMDI with spacer and face mask converts the timed spray into simple tidal breathing, maximising lower-airway deposition without requiring coordination.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "For children under 5–6 years, the correct choice is a pressurised metered-dose inhaler with a spacer and face mask, which allows medication delivery through normal tidal breathing without needing coordination."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. The pMDI with spacer and face mask is the standard-of-care device for young children, converting aerosol delivery into effortless tidal breathing."
                }
              ],
